<title>FRANCE: MATIF financial futures volume rose in October.</title>
<headline>MATIF financial futures volume rose in October.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in October rose 10.9 percent from the previous month and climbed 1.8 percent compared to October 1995, Matif said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	6.77 bln  +10.9 pct    +1.8 pct  1.13 bln</p>
<p>  Financial futures 5.46 bln   +6.4 pct    +5.2 pct   512,380</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 3.73 bln  +12.8 pct   +32.9 pct   233,784</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	 1.25 bln   -1.9 pct   -29.9 pct   216,185</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	 427,944  -12.5 pct   -24.7 pct    54,148</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	56,171  -14.0 pct   +46.4 pct     8,263</p>
<p>  Financial options 1.31 bln  +34.9 pct   -10.3 pct   620,015</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 1.08 bln  +48.3 pct   +30.7 pct   321,719</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	  214,509   -7.9 pct   -64.7 pct   290,233</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5542</p>
